 ### Added
 
+- Account e-mails: password-recovery flow — `password.request`/`password.email` (`/forgot-password`) and `password.reset`/`password.update` (`/reset-password`), guests only, with the same `status` flash on request (never reveals whether the address exists) — plus the signed e-mail verification link `verification.verify` (`/email/verify/{id}/{hash}`, `auth` + `signed` + throttled). Controllers under `app/Http/Controllers` (`app/Http/Controllers/Auth/` for verification) and views `resources/views/auth/{forgot-password,reset-password}.blade.php`.
+- Brazilian Portuguese account notifications: `ResetPassword` and `VerifyEmail` render in pt-BR ("Redefina sua senha", "Verifique seu endereço de e-mail", "Olá!", "Redefinir senha") — missing subject entries added to `lang/pt_BR.json`.
+- PegaFila markdown mail theme: `mail.markdown.theme` = `pegafila` at `resources/views/vendor/mail/html/themes/pegafila.css`, brand primary `#0f7490` on elements present in every mail (action button, header name) so it survives CSS inlining.
 - Database schema and Mermaid diagram in [`docs/database-schema.md`](docs/database-schema.md).
 - Business rules documentation in [`docs/business-rules.md`](docs/business-rules.md): MVP queue management, entity/subscription, roles (admin, owner, employee), tickets, priorities, fairness (3-ticket rule), deterministic call panel, and channels (Flutter totem, web TV, attendant).
 - This changelog (Keep a Changelog).
@@ -18,6 +21,7 @@ ### Changed
 - Documented architecture: PegaFilaWeb is a single repository for frontend, backend and totem API; Flutter remains only as a separate client.
 - Simplified model: ticket is single-use (one call; write-once except `called_at`/`called_by`) — removed `ticket_calls` table; ticket knows only its queue (no `totem_id`). `tickets.priority` is now an integer (higher = more prioritized).
 - Expanded financial model: `billing_accounts` (1:0..1 with entity) + `subscriptions` + `plans` isolate financial data. New tables: `payment_options` (cycle, method, discount, refund window) and `payments` (individual charges). `billing_accounts` has `cpf_cnpj`. Subscription 1:1 with `billing_account_id` (UK); history in `payments`. Added `tickets.code`, explicit unique constraints, and circular FK note for owner. Removed per-queue user access limit.
+- `.env.example` now ships `APP_NAME=PegaFila` and `APP_LOCALE=pt_BR` (`APP_FALLBACK_LOCALE=en`); `phpunit.xml` pins `APP_NAME`, `APP_LOCALE` and `APP_FALLBACK_LOCALE` so the test suite runs pt-BR with the PegaFila name.
 
